phase P3
title Operation kernels

tasks
    T301
        title        ResourceKeyIdentity
        status       open
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@task.Rewrite.T106, @task.Rewrite.T107]
        derives_from [@plan.Resources.O1, @plan.Resources.V1, @plan.Resources.C1]
        satisfies    [@plan.Resources.O1]
        description
            Deliver the settled canonical resource key boundary: exact key family, defensive 
            validation/copying, canonical byte identity, ordering, and key diagnostics. Ordered 
            work: (1) consume P1 T106 operation/key seams and T107 UTF-8/structural policy; (2) 
            implement only the settled key grammar and identity; (3) pin key vectors at the owning 
            test boundary. Permitted paths: packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/operation/key.ts and 
            operation/test/key.test.ts (or the existing equivalent owner); touch shared structural 
            codec only through its agreed T107 interface. Shared-write boundary: do not author 
            descriptor forms, freshness defaults, stores, or the codec core. Evidence: 
            operation/test/key.test.ts.
        acceptance
            Positive: compile and runtime vectors for equal canonical key bytes, defensive input 
            copying, ordering, and exact accepted key depth/node/byte limits behave according to 
            Resources.O1. Check: packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/operation/test/key.test.ts plus 
            `nub run --filter flow-state-rewrite check:types`; expected: exact key inference 
            compiles and equal keys share identity.

            Failure: malformed key shapes, excessive bounds, invalid UTF-8 names, and lone 
            surrogates reject before ownership or work with the canonical key diagnostic. Check: 
            operation/test/key.test.ts; expected: each invalid boundary rejects without installing 
            or mutating key state.

    T302
        title        ResourceAuthoringForms
        status       draft
        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [
                     @task.Rewrite.T106,
                     @task.Rewrite.T102,
                     @task.Rewrite.T103,
                     @T315
                     ]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.Resources.O1,
                     @plan.Resources.V1,
                     @plan.Resources.Q1,
                     @plan.Resources.C1
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.Resources.O1]
        description
            Deliver only the public resource descriptor, mapper-container, K-derived tag, and 
            placeholder forms left open by Resources.Q1, after its owner decision. Ordered work: 
            (1) record the accepted fields and exact inference for resource(config); (2) preserve 
            P/K/A/E/R through descriptor, requirement, implementation, machine, App, Runtime, 
            fixture, and Story; (3) add positive/negative compile fixtures. Permitted paths: 
            operation/resource-types.ts, operation/test/resource-types.test.ts, and owning 
            declaration/route files needed for the accepted form. Shared-write boundary: T301 owns 
            canonical key mechanics; T314 owns freshness/collection policy. This task remains draft 
            and must not be interpreted as deciding Q1.
        acceptance
            Positive: after the approved Resources.Q1 decision, exact resource fields, mapper 
            containers, tag/placeholder forms and callback types preserve P/K/A/E/R across the 
            named public graph. Check: operation/test/resource-types.test.ts and focused rewrite 
            type check; expected: only approved forms compile without widening or aliases.

            Failure: unsupported descriptor fields/forms and mismatched mapper, tag, or placeholder 
            types fail compilation. Construction performs no work. Check: 
            operation/test/resource-types.test.ts; expected: every negative fixture is rejected 
            before adapter start.

    T303
        title        CanonicalStoreAndPassiveReaders
        status       open
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@T301, @task.Rewrite.T201, @task.Rewrite.T202]
        derives_from [@plan.Resources.O2, @plan.Resources.V2, @plan.Resources.D2]
        satisfies    [@plan.Resources.O2]
        description
            Deliver one Runtime-owned canonical resource view and actor-bound passive readers over 
            it. Ordered work: (1) consume T301 key identity; (2) provide bounded canonical storage 
            and stable snapshots; (3) bind passive reads to the current actor cut; (4) prove 
            equal-key sharing and external-store behavior. Permitted paths: 
            operation/resource-store.ts, operation/resource-readers.ts, 
            operation/test/resource-store.test.ts, and focused runtime assembly wiring if required. 
            Shared-write boundary: coordinate the store port with P2 actor publication; T313 owns 
            the integrated actor/store/evidence commit cut. Do not implement host adapters or 
            operation work admission. Evidence: operation/test/resource-store.test.ts.
        acceptance
            Positive: two actors using the same canonical key observe one data view; passive reads 
            are stable, actor-bound, and perform no lookup or mutation. Check: 
            operation/test/resource-store.test.ts; expected: equal keys share committed data and 
            repeated reads are pure.

            Failure: wrong-actor or stale-cut readers cannot observe or publish another actor's 
            mutable data; structural copies do not alias caller values. Check: 
            operation/test/resource-store.test.ts; expected: rejected reads leave store and actor 
            snapshots unchanged.

            Q1-bound deferral: T318 proves placeholder projection purity after Resources.Q1 and its 
            authoring form are accepted; this Task keeps canonical reads passive and does not 
            create placeholder writes or outcomes.

    T304
        title        ResourceAcquisitionLifecycle
        status       open
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@T301, @T303, @task.Rewrite.T202, @task.Rewrite.T203]
        derives_from [@plan.Resources.O3, @plan.Resources.V3, @plan.Resources.C1]
        satisfies    [@plan.Resources.O3]
        description
            Deliver the settled resource acquisition kernel: finite admission, deduplication, 
            cancellation, current ownership, stale-result fencing, and disposal lifecycle. Ordered 
            work: (1) use T301 identity and T303 storage; (2) integrate with P2 admission and actor 
            lifecycle; (3) exercise settle/cancel/release races. Permitted paths: 
            operation/resource-lifecycle.ts and operation/test/resource-lifecycle.test.ts. 
            Shared-write boundary: freshness and collection type/default policy is T314 and remains 
            excluded until Resources.Q1 is decided; do not create omitted freshness defaults. 
            Evidence: operation/test/resource-lifecycle.test.ts.
        acceptance
            Positive: admitted lookup work is finite, equal-key consumers share only the permitted 
            in-flight occurrence, and current consumers receive a fenced settled result. Check: 
            operation/test/resource-lifecycle.test.ts; expected: current generation publishes once 
            and release/disposal is bounded.

            Failure: stale completion, cancellation, capacity refusal, or disposed ownership cannot 
            publish or mutate canonical state. Check: operation/test/resource-lifecycle.test.ts; 
            expected: rejected/stale work leaves the committed value and actor snapshot unchanged.

    T305
        title        ResourceWritesAndInvalidation
        status       open
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@T301, @T303, @task.Rewrite.T207, @task.Rewrite.T208]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.Resources.O4,
                     @plan.Resources.V4,
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.O2,
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.O3
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.Resources.O4]
        description
            Deliver authoritative explicit resource writes and bounded invalidation through the 
            single actor/store publication path. Ordered work: (1) consume the settled 
            construction-owned setData authority seam; (2) apply exact-key write and invalidation 
            batches to the canonical store; (3) publish accepted updates atomically through actor 
            actions; (4) prove overflow and stale authority failures. Permitted paths: 
            operation/resource-writes.ts, operation/test/resource-writes.test.ts, and the agreed 
            write-owner seam. Shared-write boundary: do not implement React/host adapters; 
            coordinate the shared publication integration with T313. Evidence: 
            operation/test/resource-writes.test.ts.
        acceptance
            Positive: explicit writes and bounded invalidation update the intended canonical keys 
            and publish one accepted actor/store result. Check: 
            operation/test/resource-writes.test.ts; expected: committed value, generation, and 
            actor snapshot agree after success.

            Failure: invalid authority, invalid key, capacity overflow, or rejected batch has no 
            partial effects. Check: operation/test/resource-writes.test.ts; expected: the prior 
            store value and actor/evidence sequence remain unchanged.

            Q1-bound deferral: K-derived tag expansion and its exact invalidation targets are owned 
            by T318; this Task covers exact-key, family, and other settled target forms.

    T306
        title        TransactionTypes
        status       open
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [
                     @task.Rewrite.T106,
                     @task.Rewrite.T105,
                     @task.Rewrite.T102,
                     @task.Rewrite.T103
                     ]
        derives_from [@plan.Transactions.O1, @plan.Transactions.V1, @plan.Transactions.C1]
        satisfies    [@plan.Transactions.O1]
        description
            Deliver exact finite transaction declarations, keyed inputs/results, and implementation 
            requirement closure, without selecting an omitted concurrency default. Ordered work: 
            (1) consume P1 operation-type, diagnostic, and App seams; (2) preserve exact 
            transaction input/key/success/error/service types; (3) add compile-time positive and 
            negative vectors. Permitted paths: operation/transaction-types.ts and 
            operation/test/transaction-types.test.ts. Shared-write boundary: explicit/omitted 
            policy execution belongs to T307/T308; do not edit runtime policy or preview 
            implementation. Evidence: operation/test/transaction-types.test.ts.
        acceptance
            Positive: finite transaction implementation preserves exact P, K, A, E, and R through 
            its named operation and implementation route. Check: 
            operation/test/transaction-types.test.ts; expected: accepted examples compile with no 
            widened requirement or result types.

            Failure: mismatched implementation, key, effect error, service requirement, or 
            unsupported family fails the compile fixture. Check: 
            operation/test/transaction-types.test.ts; expected: every negative fixture is rejected.

    T307
        title        ExplicitConcurrencyPolicies
        status       open
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@T306, @T303, @task.Rewrite.T202, @task.Rewrite.T203]
        derives_from [@plan.Transactions.O2, @plan.Transactions.V2, @plan.Transactions.D1]
        satisfies    [@plan.Transactions.O2]
        description
            Deliver actor-local exact-key transaction occurrences for each explicitly authored 
            concurrency policy. Ordered work: (1) consume T306 transaction types and T303 canonical 
            store; (2) apply the explicitly selected policy to same-key operations; (3) prove 
            serialization/fencing, lifecycle release, and distinct-key independence. Permitted 
            paths: operation/transaction-concurrency.ts and 
            operation/test/transaction-concurrency.test.ts. Shared-write boundary: do not pick the 
            omitted default; T308 owns Q2. Do not integrate persistence reconciliation here; 
            T310/T404 own the local/remote uncertainty distinction. Evidence: 
            operation/test/transaction-concurrency.test.ts.
        acceptance
            Positive: explicit policies produce their specified same-key ordering and distinct-key 
            independence while keeping occurrences actor-local. Check: 
            operation/test/transaction-concurrency.test.ts; expected: each authored policy settles 
            in its defined order and only its current occurrence publishes.

            Failure: cancellation, stale generation, actor disposal, and replacement do not let an 
            older occurrence overwrite the current result. Check: 
            operation/test/transaction-concurrency.test.ts; expected: prior/current state follows 
            the authored policy and no stale publication occurs.

    T308
        title        OmittedConcurrencyDefault
        status       draft
        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [@T307, @T316]
        derives_from [@plan.Transactions.O2, @plan.Transactions.V2, @plan.Transactions.Q2]
        satisfies    [@plan.Transactions.O2]
        description
            After Transactions.Q2 is decided, implement and verify the default used when a 
            transaction omits its optional concurrency policy. Ordered work: (1) encode the 
            approved default as a closed type/runtime rule; (2) show omitted and explicit forms are 
            distinguished exactly; (3) add behavior vectors for same-key, distinct-key, and 
            cancellation cases. Permitted paths: transaction policy owner and 
            operation/test/transaction-concurrency.test.ts. Shared-write boundary: does not block 
            explicit policy work in T307 or settled store/preview work. This task remains draft and 
            must not infer Q2 from existing source. This Task remains draft until the local 
            Transactions.Q2 decision Task T316 resolves the omitted-field policy.
        acceptance
            Positive: omitted policy follows only the approved Transactions.Q2 default, while every 
            explicit policy retains its own behavior. Check: 
            operation/test/transaction-concurrency.test.ts; expected: omitted-policy cases match 
            the decision table.

            Failure: invalid policy values or forms reject before admission or mutation. Check: 
            operation/test/transaction-concurrency.test.ts plus transaction type fixtures; 
            expected: no operation starts and canonical diagnostic/type rejection is observed.

    T309
        title        TransactionPreviewsAndCAS
        status       open
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@T303, @T305, @T306]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.Transactions.O3,
                     @plan.Transactions.V3,
                     @plan.Resources.O2,
                     @plan.Resources.O4
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.Transactions.O3]
        description
            Deliver isolated transaction previews and canonical compare-and-set settlement. Ordered 
            work: (1) read an immutable actor/store basis; (2) produce preview output without 
            committing; (3) settle explicit writes only through CAS against the captured 
            generation; (4) prove stacked previews and losing races. Permitted paths: 
            operation/transaction-preview.ts and operation/test/transaction-preview.test.ts. 
            Shared-write boundary: compose with T303 store and T305 write owner; previews must not 
            mutate data or publish evidence. Do not choose omitted concurrency default. Evidence: 
            operation/test/transaction-preview.test.ts.
        acceptance
            Positive: previews see committed basis and return isolated results; a winning CAS 
            publishes once through the canonical store. Check: 
            operation/test/transaction-preview.test.ts; expected: preview leaves committed data 
            unchanged and the accepted write advances the intended generation.

            Failure: stale generation, failed transaction, or losing CAS changes no canonical value 
            and emits no partial publication. Check: operation/test/transaction-preview.test.ts; 
            expected: prior data/snapshot remain intact and the losing outcome is explicit.

    T310
        title        RemoteCancellationTruth
        status       open
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@T307, @T309, @task.Rewrite.T203]
        derives_from [@plan.Transactions.O4, @plan.Transactions.V4, @plan.Transactions.D2]
        satisfies    [@plan.Transactions.O4]
        description
            Deliver truthful cancellation and uncertainty at the remote-effect boundary. Ordered 
            work: (1) distinguish queued work from a started remote invocation; (2) cancel queued 
            work without side effects; (3) retain unknown/reconcile-required truth when an invoked 
            remote effect may have committed; (4) fence stale completion and preserve current actor 
            state. Permitted paths: operation/transaction-remote.ts and 
            operation/test/transaction-remote.test.ts. Shared-write boundary: persistence 
            normalization on restore belongs to T404; coordinate the status facts consumed there. 
            No replay is permitted. Evidence: operation/test/transaction-remote.test.ts.
        acceptance
            Positive: queued cancellation leaves state untouched; a started remote invocation 
            reports success/failure only when known, otherwise exposes the specified 
            unknown/reconcile-required state. Check: operation/test/transaction-remote.test.ts; 
            expected: outcome reflects the invocation boundary.

            Failure: late completion after cancel/replacement/disposal cannot publish stale local 
            data or claim a remote rollback. Check: operation/test/transaction-remote.test.ts; 
            expected: current state remains fenced and remote uncertainty remains explicit.

            Remote-journal gate: for an invoked adapter, distinguish adapter invocation from remote 
            dispatch. A pending or failed independent durable journal acknowledgment prevents any 
            remote request; after acknowledgment, cancellation remains unknown/reconcileRequired 
            unless the adapter evidence rules out dispatch. Check: 
            operation/test/transaction-remote.test.ts; expected: request count is zero before/after 
            failed acknowledgment, and no Flow Persistence provider or persist:false transaction 
            changes that journal rule.

    T311
        title        StreamSessionsAndRelease
        status       open
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [
                     @task.Rewrite.T106,
                     @task.Rewrite.T102,
                     @task.Rewrite.T202,
                     @task.Rewrite.T203,
                     @task.Rewrite.T209
                     ]
        derives_from [@plan.Streams.O2, @plan.Streams.V2, @plan.Streams.D1]
        satisfies    [@plan.Streams.O2, @plan.Statecharts.O4]
        description
            Deliver stream session identity, latest projections, actor/runtime ownership, and 
            release behavior independent of the unresolved public mapper container. Ordered work: 
            (1) consume operation/action and Statechart lifecycle seams; (2) bind one declared 
            stream occurrence to its current actor ownership; (3) publish latest values through 
            accepted actions; (4) prove replacement, terminal, and disposal release. Permitted 
            paths: operation/stream-lifecycle.ts and operation/test/stream-lifecycle.test.ts. 
            Shared-write boundary: T312 owns authoring form; T414 owns durable 
            projection/hydration; stream session work must not wait for either. Evidence: 
            operation/test/stream-lifecycle.test.ts.
        acceptance
            Positive: equal declaration identity acquires and publishes the current stream 
            projection under the declared lifetime, and release occurs on 
            replacement/terminal/disposal. Check: operation/test/stream-lifecycle.test.ts; 
            expected: one current session and deterministic release.

            Failure: replaced or released sessions cannot publish later values or retain 
            Runtime/actor ownership. Check: operation/test/stream-lifecycle.test.ts; expected: late 
            emissions are ignored and disposal completes without leaked session activity.

    T312
        title        StreamAuthoringForms
        status       draft
        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [
                     @task.Rewrite.T106,
                     @task.Rewrite.T102,
                     @task.Rewrite.T103,
                     @task.Rewrite.T108,
                     @T317
                     ]
        derives_from [@plan.Streams.O1, @plan.Streams.V1, @plan.Streams.Q1, @plan.Streams.C1]
        satisfies    [@plan.Streams.O1]
        description
            After Streams.Q1 is decided, implement only the approved stream descriptor, adapter 
            return, and mapper-container forms. Ordered work: (1) record accepted exact P/K/V/E/R 
            types and named projections; (2) preserve them through machine/App/Runtime/fixtures; 
            (3) pin positive and negative fixtures. Permitted paths: operation/stream-types.ts, 
            operation/test/stream-types.test.ts, and public declaration routes for the approved 
            forms. Shared-write boundary: T311 session lifetime behavior proceeds independently; no 
            guessed adapter or mapper form. This task remains draft. The local Streams.Q1 decision 
            is recorded in T317; this Task does not select a form.
        acceptance
            Positive: approved declaration and adapter forms preserve exact P/K/V/E/R inference 
            through named routes. Check: operation/test/stream-types.test.ts and focused type 
            check; expected: only the approved forms compile.

            Failure: unsupported return/container forms or mismatched event/data/error/requirement 
            types reject. Check: operation/test/stream-types.test.ts; expected: negative fixtures 
            fail with no added public aliases.

    T313
        title        ActorStoreEvidencePublicationCut
        status       open
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@task.Rewrite.T210, @T303, @T305, @T307, @T309, @T310, @T311]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.O2,
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.O3,
                     @plan.Resources.O2,
                     @plan.Resources.O4,
                     @plan.Transactions.O2,
                     @plan.Transactions.O3,
                     @plan.Transactions.O4,
                     @plan.Streams.O2,
                     @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.O7,
                     @plan.Statecharts.O3,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O3,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.V3
                     ]
        satisfies    [
                     @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.O7,
                     @plan.Statecharts.O3,
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.O3
                     ]
        description
            Integrate actor turns, canonical resource/transaction/stream changes, and evidence 
            acceptance at one production publication owner. This is the P3 cut, not a persistence 
            implementation. Ordered work: (1) align actor action and T303 store preparation; (2) 
            include T305 write settlement, T307/T309/T310 transaction facts, and T311 stream facts; 
            (3) make one committed current cut observable to store readers and evidence; (4) prove 
            acknowledgment follows evidence acceptance and failures roll back only prepared state. 
            Permitted paths: runtime-next actor/store publication owner and 
            runtime-next/test/operation-publication-cut.test.ts. Shared-write boundary: this is the 
            only P3 integration writer for the cut; operation owners provide their seams without 
            parallel actor/store/evidence semantics. No P2 T205 dependency unless acceptance 
            expands to causal context-wave behavior. Evidence: operation-publication-cut.test.ts.
        acceptance
            Positive: one operation action commits actor snapshot, canonical store projection, and 
            evidence at the same sequence/cut; acknowledgment occurs after evidence acceptance. 
            Check: runtime-next/test/operation-publication-cut.test.ts; expected: readers, 
            snapshots, and accepted evidence describe the same commit.

            Failure: pre-commit validation, store prepare, capacity, or evidence rejection leaves 
            actor and store at the previous cut and emits no acknowledgment; post-commit listener 
            failure cannot roll back a committed cut. Check: 
            runtime-next/test/operation-publication-cut.test.ts; expected: failure lane and 
            sequence match the commit boundary.

            Integration coverage includes one resource write, one transaction settlement, one 
            stream projection/release, and passive reads from the integrated production owner. 
            Check: runtime-next/test/operation-publication-cut.test.ts; expected: each operation 
            uses the same actor/store/evidence authority.

            Explicit Q1 deferral: placeholder projection and K-derived tag expansion are owned by 
            T318 after Resources.Q1; this gate proves settled store/write/publication paths and 
            does not imply those metadata forms are complete.

    T314
        title        ResourceFreshnessPolicy
        status       draft
        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [@T301, @T303, @T304, @T315]
        derives_from [@plan.Resources.O3, @plan.Resources.V3, @plan.Resources.Q1]
        satisfies    [@plan.Resources.O3]
        description
            After Resources.Q1 is decided, implement the exact staleTime/gcTime domains and omitted 
            freshness/collection behavior. Ordered work: (1) encode only the accepted descriptor 
            types and defaults; (2) apply them to acquisition/retention without changing settled 
            identity or passive reader semantics; (3) prove freshness, collection, and replacement 
            races. Permitted paths: resource descriptor/lifecycle owner and 
            operation/test/resource-lifecycle.test.ts. Shared-write boundary: T304 must remain 
            runnable without these defaults; this task does not block store, writes, or transaction 
            tasks. This task remains draft and must not infer Q1 from old source. The local 
            Resources.Q1 decision is recorded in T315; this Task does not invent a default.
        acceptance
            Positive: authored freshness/collection values and omitted forms follow the approved 
            Resources.Q1 decision across acquisition and retention. Check: 
            operation/test/resource-lifecycle.test.ts; expected: generation and retention 
            transitions match the decision table.

            Failure: invalid durations or stale acquisition cannot replace current data. Check: 
            operation/test/resource-lifecycle.test.ts; expected: rejection occurs before 
            mutation/work and the last committed value remains.

    T315
        title        Resolve resource metadata and freshness authoring forms
        status       draft
        priority     medium
        derives_from [@plan.Resources.Q1, @plan.ProjectDelivery.O4]
        description
            Resolve every Resources.Q1 clause in the owning capability Plan: accepted K-derived tag 
            and placeholder fields/containers/callbacks, finite and continuing mapper containers, 
            staleTime/gcTime input domains, Infinity, and omitted policy behavior. Preserve 
            already-settled descriptor, key, passive-reader, and explicit-write commitments. This 
            is a local decision task; unrelated resource key/store/acquisition work continues.
        acceptance
            Record an explicit owner-approved answer for each Q1 clause, with exact 
            positive/negative API consequences, before T302/T314 implementation. Do not infer 
            defaults or legacy forms. No source implementation belongs to this decision Task.

