    T318
        title        Resource metadata projection and tag invalidation
        status       draft
        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [@T302, @T303, @T305, @T315]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.Resources.O2,
                     @plan.Resources.V2,
                     @plan.Resources.O4,
                     @plan.Resources.V4,
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.O2
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.Resources.O2, @plan.Resources.O4]
        description
            After Resources.Q1 and T302 settle the exact metadata forms, integrate K-derived tags 
            and descriptor-owned placeholders without changing settled store/acquisition/write 
            authority. Ordered work: (1) project placeholders purely from descriptor metadata with 
            no canonical write, family, or mapped outcome; (2) index accepted tags from canonical 
            keys; (3) validate and expand tag invalidation against one pre-mutation index in stable 
            insertion order under the existing batch bound. Permitted paths: 
            operation/resource-types.ts, operation/resource-store.ts, operation/resource-writes.ts, 
            and focused resource type/store/write tests. Shared-write boundary: T302 owns authoring 
            forms; T303 owns canonical base/readers; T305 owns exact/family writes and the 
            actor/store commit path. This Task stays draft pending T315 and local tag/placeholder 
            decisions.
        acceptance
            Positive: approved placeholder metadata projects to passive reads without canonical 
            storage, family, revision, or mapped outcome; K-derived tags expand to the exact 
            matching identities in stable first-seen order. Check: resource type/store/write tests; 
            expected: projection is pure and expansion uses the accepted pre-mutation index.

            Failure: malformed or unauthorized tag target, conflicting mixed target, or expansion 
            above 256 identities rejects the whole action before mutation/work; caller mutation 
            cannot change indexed tags or projected values. Check: resource write tests; expected: 
            no partial invalidation and prior canonical data remains unchanged.
